= Introduction <intro>

This document is a guided tour of `mos-lsp`, the Mosaic language server. It is
also an ordinary document: the headings are numbered and the prose cross-links
to them. Section @features lists what the server can do, section @setup covers
installation, and the closing remarks sit in section @conclusion on page
@page(conclusion).

Each cross-reference above prints as a number in the PDF, but in the `.mos`
source it is a live `@label` reference. That duality is the whole point: readers
of the PDF get clean section numbers, while an editor wired to `mos-lsp` can
navigate and rename the same references in the source.

= Language server features <features>

`mos-lsp` ships three capabilities today:

- Diagnostics surface compiler errors as you edit.
- Go-to-definition jumps from a reference to the heading that declares its label.
- Rename rewrites a label's declaration and every reference together.

Citations resolve too: the nod to the classic typesetting manual [@knuth1984]
and the bibliography-style reference [@patashnik1988] print as numbered markers.

== Go-to-definition <gotodef>

Go-to-definition jumps from a reference to the heading that declares its label.
This section demonstrates it on itself: it holds a live reference to its own
heading — section @gotodef — which the PDF prints as the number you see. In the
source that token is `@gotodef`; put the cursor on it and run go-to-definition to
land on this heading's `<gotodef>` label.

== Rename <rename>

Rename rewrites a label's declaration and every reference to it in one edit. This
heading declares the `<rename>` label, and the cross-link here —
section @rename — is a reference to it. Rename either the declaration or this reference,
and both change together, in view, without scrolling away from this section.

== Diagnostics <diagnostics>

To watch diagnostics appear, introduce an error in the source: point a reference
at a label that does not exist, or cite an unknown bibliography key. `mos-lsp`
reports the problem inline; undo to clear it.

= Setup <setup>

Install the server so it lands on `PATH` — run `cargo mosils` from the
workspace — then open this project in your editor. Section @intro has the
overview and section @conclusion has the final check.

= Conclusion <conclusion>

If go-to-definition reached this heading from a reference, rename swept a label
cleanly, and the page printed for section @conclusion matches where you are
reading, the language server is wired correctly.
